      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"4\">Level 4 - Advanced</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">85 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Build it yourself: 90 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Machine-coding case study</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Rank 32 of the LLD question list</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>In-Memory Key-Value Store (TTL, Transactions)</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">\"Build a tiny Redis\" is a favourite running-code round at Uber, Razorpay and Salesforce because it looks easy and is not: keys that expire on time without a thread per key, <code>BEGIN / COMMIT / ROLLBACK</code> that nest, snapshots you can restore (the Memento pattern), and many threads reading and writing at once without lost updates. This page builds all of it in Java, Python and C++14, with every design choice explained.</p>\n"
  },
